DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     vveellnneett extracts the CONNECTIVITY of drawings made with
     vveelllluumm: wires unioned by endpoint, junction dots joined,
     symbol pins attached, nets named.  The four forms below are
     four ways of writing down the same walk, so a netlist and a
     parts list can never disagree with each other.

     Every form takes the sheet SET: named nets merge across
     sheets (a net called VBUS on sheet 1 is the same conductor
     as VBUS on sheet 3), and a design gets ONE parts list.  The
     file name - is standard input.

     TThhee nneettlliisstt (nnoo ooppttiioonn)
     One line per net, with R1.2-style pins; a library that NAMES
     its pins prints Q1.B instead.  GGNNDD and VVCCCC stencils and NN
     net-name markers name nets.  Designator-less stencils
     (rails, taps, off-page markers) carry nets but are never
     listed as pins.  Single-pin nets and unconnected pins are
     warned about on standard error; to make them FAIL a build,
     use vveellcchheecckk.

     -bboomm
     The bill of materials over the whole set: count, stencil,
     value and the designators, sorted.  A designated part with
     no value prints its value as ``-'' - and is a finding in
     vveellcchheecckk, which is where that belongs.

     -ssppiiccee
     A SPICE 2G6 deck on standard output: the same nets as the
     netlist, numbered (0 for the GND-named net), one card per
     designated R/C/L/D/Q.  Values are parsed from the value
     field - ``4k7'', ``100n'', ``2.2M'' - where the suffix let-
     ter doubles as the decimal point, and the schematic's M
     emits as MEG.  A D or Q card ends with its stencil CODE as
     the model name unless its value names one.  Pin ORDER is the
     library's, except that a library which NAMES its pins B/C/E
     (or A/K) orders the card the way SPICE wants; the stock
     ddiissccrreettee library does.

     Everything the subset cannot say is SKIPPED AND COUNTED on
     standard error (``dropped: 1 OPA, 2 J''): a silent partial
     netlist is how simulations lie.  Models are yours by design
     - the deck ends .EENNDD and a wrapper file .IINNCCLLUUDDEE ss it beside
     the .MMOODDEELL lines.

     -rreennuumm


