     Canonical designators: symbols sorted by (y, x), numbered
     per prefix from -bbaassee _n (default 1), and the whole drawing
     re-emitted on standard output.  Designators live nowhere
     else in the format - nets are positional - so the rewrite
     cannot dangle a reference.  ONE sheet per run; a set renum-
     bers sheet by sheet with -bbaassee carrying the count across,
     because the Makefile owns the set.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
                  velnet amp1.d amp2.d
                  velnet -bom amp?.d > parts.txt
                  velnet -spice amp?.d > deck.cir
                  velnet -renum -base 1 amp1.d > new.d && mv new.d amp1.d

